# API route conventions

- Wrap every handler with `withAuth(withErrorHandler(handler as any))` from `@/lib/auth`.
  - `withAuth` provides user + company + transaction GUCs.
  - The legacy `withCompany` is removed (GoTrue cutover) — do NOT use it.
- For role-gated routes, compose `withRole(...)` inside `withAuth`.
- For pure JWT-verify routes (no company scope), use `withUserAuth`.

## Response shape

Use the `apiResponse` helpers from `@/lib/apiResponse`:

- `apiResponse.success(res, data)`
- `apiResponse.badRequest(res, msg)`
- `apiResponse.notFound(res, msg)`
- `apiResponse.methodNotAllowed(res)`

Clients always unwrap `json.data.<field>` — never return raw JSON.

## DB

- `sql` tagged template from `@/lib/neon` (legacy path; runtime is pg).
- Every query MUST include `WHERE company_id = ${companyId}`.
- Never string-concat queries; never interpolate user input outside `${}` placeholders.

## Logging

- Use `log.error / log.info / log.warn` from `@/lib/logger`.
- NEVER `console.log` (Zero Tolerance violation).
- No empty `catch` blocks — log and re-throw or handle.
